---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { localizedPath } from '../../i18n';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  title="Pelerin privacy policy — Luvita"
  description="Privacy policy of the Pelerin desktop app: it runs on your computer and sends nothing to Luvita."
  paths={{ tr: 'pelerin-gizlilik', en: 'pelerin-privacy' }}
>
  <Hero eyebrow="Legal" title="Pelerin: privacy policy" />

  <section class="container">
    <Prose>
      <p>Version 0.1 · Last updated: 5 October 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Pelerin is made by Luvita. Contact:
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What the app does</h2>
      <p>
        Pelerin runs on your own computer. You paste text into it. It finds
        personal identifiers in that text (for example names, ID numbers, IBANs
        and phone numbers) and replaces them with placeholders. You can copy the
        masked text into another tool yourself. If you paste an answer back, the
        app puts the original values back in, on your screen.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What we collect: nothing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not receive, copy, store or see the text you paste, the masked
        text, the placeholders or the original values. The app has no account, no
        sign-in, no analytics and no telemetry. It does not send anything to
        Luvita.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Where your text goes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The app's own engine, on your computer.</strong> The window you
          see is served by an engine that runs on the same computer and listens
          only on that computer's loopback address. Nothing outside your computer
          can reach it. A new access code is created for every launch and is held
          in memory only.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Nothing else.</strong> The app makes no connection to any AI
          service, to Luvita or to any other server. It never sends your text
          anywhere. Anything you do with the masked text afterwards, such as
          pasting it into an AI tool, is your own act.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The original values live in memory only.</strong> The table that
          links each placeholder to its original value is held in the engine's
          memory and is gone when you close the app.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. What stays on your computer</h2>
      <p>
        The app writes a few files on your computer. They contain no text you
        pasted and no original values.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>A record of placeholders</strong>
          (<code>Pelerin\audit\…\records.jsonl</code>): one line for each
          placeholder issued, with its placeholder code (for example a type name
          and a number), the time, and technical hashes. It shows how many
          identifiers of which types were found in a request. It never contains
          the text or the original values.
        </li>
        <li>A small usage counter file next to it.</li>
        <li>
          Temporary working files of the engine, in a folder under
          <code>C:\ProgramData</code> whose name starts with <code>pd</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          The window's browser profile (cache and settings of the Microsoft Edge
          WebView2 component that draws the window), in
          <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\dev.cosmocrew.pelerin.desktop</code>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you uninstall the app from the Microsoft Store, the app's own folder
        is removed. The <code>C:\ProgramData\pd…</code> folder and the browser
        profile folder can stay behind. You can delete them yourself at any time.
        We do not read them.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Microsoft and Windows</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime.</strong> The app needs this
          Windows component to draw its window (Windows 11 and updated Windows 10
          already include it). It is a Microsoft product with its own behaviour
          and may connect to Microsoft services. We do not control that.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Microsoft Store.</strong> Microsoft collects installation and
          usage information about Store apps and gives us reports in aggregate,
          such as how many people installed the app and failure counts with
          technical stack traces. We use these reports only to keep the app
          working. Microsoft's own privacy statement governs what Microsoft
          collects.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Crash reports.</strong> If the app stops unexpectedly, Windows
          Error Reporting may keep or send a crash report to Microsoft, depending
          on your Windows diagnostic data settings. Such a report could include
          information that was in the app's memory at that moment. If you handle
          sensitive text, check your Windows diagnostic data settings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. What you do with masked text</h2>
      <p>
        Pelerin keeps raw identifiers on your computer and materially reduces the
        risk of re-identification, disclosure and breach in the text you send
        onward. It does not mean that no personal data leaves your computer, and
        it does not remove your own obligations. If you send masked text to a
        service outside Türkiye, the legal basis for that transfer under Article
        9 of the Turkish Personal Data Protection Law (KVKK, Law No. 6698) is
        still yours to provide.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>
        The engine listens on your computer only, uses a per-launch access code
        held in memory, and keeps the original values in memory only. No system is
        perfectly secure, and the files listed in section 5 are protected only as
        well as your own Windows account and disk.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because we do not receive or hold the text you handle with the app, we
        hold no such personal data about you. If you write to us, we use your
        message only to answer it; see our
        <a href={localizedPath('en', 'privacy')}>website privacy policy</a>. For data Microsoft holds
        about you, contact Microsoft. If you are in Türkiye you have the rights
        listed in Article 11 of KVKK, and you can ask us about them at
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Children</h2>
      <p>Pelerin is not made for children.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We will publish changes to this policy at this address and change the
        date above. A change that affects what the app does with your data will
        come with a new version of the app.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
